UNIT parse_wire
LANG ts
PRIMARY-SHA256 4c4e81554252a1204b31465947429f7ed248b5f7d92b440fde8d9c576c9ef1a6
SIG export default function parse_wire(line: string): Wire
ABI TypeScript compiles to the js runtime and is driven exactly as js. Declare in the artifact
  type Wire = null | boolean | number | bigint | string | readonly Wire[] | { readonly [key: string]: Wire }
  text = string (UTF-16; a lone surrogate is representable); f64 = number (double; -0 preserved); the exact integer of R6 =
  bigint; bool = boolean; none = null; list = an array; map = a plain object with OWN entries ("__proto__" is an own key).
  STRICT: the artifact type-checks under strict: true with no any, no non-null assertions (!), no @ts-ignore and no
  @ts-expect-error. A throw (R1, R5, R8, OUT-OF-DOMAIN) is a thrown Error; the message is not graded. ES module default
  export; imports nothing.
ENVELOPE widening as js: results holding a bigint (R6) or a lone surrogate (R3), and non-string arguments at runtime (OUT-OF-DOMAIN: a
  throw, never converted with String()).
MECHANISM (restated from js — language files are self-contained) a hand-written recursive-descent reader over the string's
  UTF-16 code units, each numeral kept as its source text. Do NOT use JSON.parse: on the authority's Node 24.16 it carries a
  key cache across calls (after a key that is one backslash, a later one-escape key such as "\t" reads back as the
  backslash), and the oracle holds exactly that sequence of lines; it also yields Infinity where R5 throws and has no R8
  limit. Number(text) realizes the R5 rounding. R6: for an INTEGER-SPELLING numeral whose Number is not a safe integer,
  return BigInt(text) unless the Number is finite and BigInt(Number) equals it. Build maps with Object.defineProperty so
  "__proto__" is own. OUT-OF-DOMAIN: throw first when typeof line is not
  'string'; the typed parameter is still string.
DEPENDS-ON none
PINNED regex INTEGER-SPELLING = /^-?[0-9]+$/ CITED R6 — no fraction, no exponent; tested on the numeral's source text
PINNED regex NUMERAL = /^-?(?:0|[1-9][0-9]*)(?:\.[0-9]+)?(?:[eE][+-]?[0-9]+)?/ CITED R1 R5 — matched at the read position
PROVENANCE rederive@f68cca701417 cli/lang/rust.mjs parseWire (byte-identical to 1d1861440f2c and 6199e2cc8b75). Language file re-cut 2026-10-27 with the primary; round-5b delta (FINDINGS #120).
